# Keeps the Docker build context to what the build actually needs.
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING LINE IS `dist/`. Without it a developer's stale dist/ enters the
# context, deploy/Dockerfile's backend stage does `COPY . .` so that old dist/ lands in
# /build/dist, mage only ADDS gpx_* binaries beside the files already there, and the
# runtime stage copies --from=backend SECOND -- so the stale plugin.json overwrites the
# one webpack just built. The image then reports an old plugin version with no error
# anywhere. Observed: package.json 0.1.1, a local dist/ left at 0.0.10, image built
# locally reporting 0.0.10. CI never sees it because a clean checkout has no dist/,
# which is exactly why it stays hidden.
#
# .git/ is deliberately NOT excluded: Go stamps version-control information into the
# binary from it, and dropping it silently changes what `go version -m` reports on the
# shipped gpx_* binaries.
dist/
node_modules/

# Build and test artefacts that only bloat the context.
artifacts/
work/
ci/
pkg-root/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
*.zip
*.sha1

# Never ship these into a build context: .env holds local credentials and
# docs/internal/ is gitignored because this repository is public.
.env
docs/internal/
